==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|haldan}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|haldanan||to watch, look after|lang=gem-pro}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''[[halda]]'', Old Saxon ''[[haldan]]'' (Dutch ''[[houden]]''), Old High German ''[[haltan]]'' (German ''[[halten]]''), Old Norse ''[[halda]]'' (Swedish ''[[hålla]]''), Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐌻𐌳𐌰𐌽|sc=Goth}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhæɑldɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VII}}

# to keep watch over (cattle etc.)
# to [[hold]] fast, to [[grasp]]
# to [[contain]]
# to [[possess]]
# {{intransitive|lang=ang}} to maintain one’s position against an enemy

